{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfrj6f64DLRs3HenMDJuz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled **DISMISS not-worth-cost** on ROUNDS: the defect is real, but it only ever blocks, and the proper fix belongs in its own work item. The verdict is in `docs/reviews/wi-853-findings-gate-in-rework/006-ADJUDICATE-349bb13.md`, committed as `8ab89b47` with the trailer `WI: WI-853`; the commit hooks passed.\n\n**Reproduction:** I built the reviewer's case in a scratch test outside the repo, reusing the lane's own test fixtures. I've deleted it since.\n- An accepted DISMISS of F2, with its findings file beside the verdict, exits 0.\n- Add an earlier round's findings file that also requests F2 but records a different finding, and the same plan exits 1. The message is \"whose finding F2 is not this review's F2\".\n- An exclusion that gives its reason without citing the verdict path exits 0.\n\n**Why dismiss rather than fix:**\n- **It only blocks.** No unresolved finding gets through. Two disagreeing candidate files is a finding that \"cannot be shown\", which SR-236 already says to refuse. The Done-when's \"a resolved dispute passes\" holds, and is tested, for the normal single-round case.\n- **The cost is one refused gate run.** Keeping dispute ids unique within a lane clears it, and so does an exclusion that doesn't cite the verdict.\n- **The real fix is bigger than the defect.** I agree with the coordinator that the only sound fix is to record which findings file the sitting read in the verdict's `.requested` record. Accepting any agreeing file would reopen the hole round 1 found. But that fix changes `kitlib/sitting` (SR-232/LLR-310) and the brief composer and entry point (SR-234/LLR-315), and it would need another sitting and another full-lane review. That's two other approved requirement chains outside this item's Done-when.\n\n**What the coordinator should know:**\n- **The skill doesn't state the workaround.** At this range the session-protocol skill only describes the refusal. It never tells coordinators to keep dispute ids unique within a lane, contrary to the coordinator's position. The follow-up should add that.\n- **Follow-up to file:** have the entry point record the findings file in the `.requested` record when it reserves the sitting, have `plan_coverage` read exactly that file, and refuse older records that lack it.\n- **A gap I noted but didn't rule on:** a disputed finding can be excluded with prose that never cites its verdict, and the gate accepts it like any other reasoned exclusion. SR-236 only constrains exclusions that do cite a ruling. It's worth weighing in the same follow-up.\n\nI didn't touch any code, registry, review or findings file. The coordinator's `.requested` marker is still untracked and I left it alone."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4016,"cache_read_input_tokens":111027,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4016},"output_tokens":717,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1fb1008-6d93-4693-a49f-a0783f483182","uuid":"8a03da10-f0b8-4ac4-b549-f0a4f941c5e8","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:16:43.696Z","request_id":"req_011Cfrj6eLu6ukw8RHZCU7GD"}
